1 NOTE First husband of [[leontine_schreel]]. `doc`, because the evidence is the same document
2 CONT that carries her: [[edouard_dk]]'s Oostende marriage act of 9 May 1946, read as an image,
2 CONT which describes his bride as divorced from Benoni Joseph Rossel.
2 CONT
2 CONT That is the whole of him. The act names him to establish that Leontine was free to marry,
2 CONT not to say anything about him, so there are no dates, no places and no parents — and
2 CONT nothing here justifies inventing any. Neither the wedding nor the divorce is dated in it,
2 CONT which is why his entry below carries neither.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is at the far edge of this tree: the first husband of the second wife of a man who
2 CONT married into the family. No line of descent runs through him, and none ever will.
2 CONT FRONTIER — the Schreel–Rossel marriage and divorce acts, both West-Vlaanderen civil
2 CONT registration, which would date the marriage and give his parents.
