1 NOTE CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father, by his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of
2 CONT 20 June 1872, which names the bride's parents as Guilielmus Bossin and Anna Catharina
2 CONT Peremans.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026): named in his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872 as
2 CONT *landbouwer*, living at Kraainem — an occupation this record did not have.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (2026-07-26): his own marriage act — Zaventem nr. 1, 24 February 1846 (S19),
2 CONT read as an image. He married [[peremans]] there, and the act states he was **born at
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, was **21 years old**, and worked as an *arbeider*. The age puts his
2 CONT birth in 1824 or early 1825, confirming from a civil act the 1824 this record had carried
2 CONT from a member tree; the birthplace is new, and the *landbouwer* of 1872 was a labourer at
2 CONT twenty-one.
2 CONT
2 CONT It also names his parents, [[arnoldus_bossin]] and [[elisabeth_deyn]] of
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, both present at the wedding, both consenting, and neither able to
2 CONT write. They are recorded here from this act.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (2026-07-26): he appears again as a **witness at his sister's wedding** —
2 CONT [[anna_maria_bossin]], Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). The bride's
2 CONT parents are named identically to his own, and he is there in person, so this tree gains
2 CONT his sister and he gains a sibling.
2 CONT
2 CONT **It also dates him twice over.** He is **29** on 1 December 1853, which places his birth
2 CONT between December 1823 and December 1824; his own act made him **21** on 24 February 1846,
2 CONT which places it between February 1824 and February 1825. The two windows overlap only in
2 CONT **1824, between late February and early December** — two acts, seven years apart, agreeing
2 CONT on a year this record had been carrying from a member tree alone.
2 CONT
2 CONT His trade moves with him: *arbeider* at twenty-one, *steenslager* at twenty-nine,
2 CONT *landbouwer* of Kraainem by 1872. He was living at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, where he was born,
2 CONT in 1853.
