1 NOTE Source detail: Family memory (Roland’s father). Documentary lead: = Gustavus-Josephus Dekeyser b.1899 (stefpaelinck tree, Oostende), Jerome’s brother — unconfirmed
2 CONT
2 CONT CONFIRMED placement: Cosette confirms Jerome is Roland’s GRANDFATHER, so Gustaaf is Jerome & Léonie’s son — a younger brother of Albert (1920–1972), born ~1920–1928 in Oostende. (This rules out the earlier idea that he was Jerome’s brother Gustavus-Josephus b.1899.) He & Simonne were in England during WWII, where Roland was born in 1943 (plus a daughter). UNCERTAIN: Shaun wondered whether Gustaaf may have died during the war (perhaps in Belgium or France) — but he’s not sure, so this is only a possibility to check, NOT established. He simply isn’t in Belgian civil indexes for a Gustave Dekeyser born ~1920s Oostende, which fits either a wartime death abroad OR a life lived mostly outside Belgium. Open leads to chase next (they’d resolve his fate either way): (1) Roland’s 1943 birth certificate — England & Wales GRO, Edmonton registration district, Q3/Q4 1943, surname De Keyser/Dekeyser, mother’s maiden name Vandewalle (via FreeBMD/GRO); (2) a UK marriage of Gustaaf × Simonne, 1940–43; (3) UK death indexes for a Gustave De Keyser; (4) if he served, Free Belgian Forces / Brigade Piron rolls; (5) Belgian war-dead databases (bel-memorial.org; De Plate Oostende heemkring) — only relevant IF he died in the war.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHECKED, AND THE CORPUS DOES NOT HAVE HIM (July 2026). His best candidates score 27 bits
2 CONT and are **Josse De Keyser of Aalst, 1809**, **Petrus De Keyser of Aalst, 1840**, and an
2 CONT Alphonse De Keyser at Leuven in 1952. The first two are a century out and in the wrong
2 CONT province; none has a date or place in common with him.
2 CONT
2 CONT The score comes from the surname plus a shared forename among children, which for De Keyser
2 CONT in Oost-Vlaanderen is close to no information at all. This is a clean negative: the open
2 CONT Belgian corpus as harvested so far holds nothing that could be Gustaaf, which is consistent
2 CONT with what his record already suspects — that his adult life, and possibly his death, happened
2 CONT outside Belgium.
2 CONT
2 CONT The leads that matter are still the English ones listed above.
1 SOUR @S51@
2 QUAY 2
