1 NOTE Mother of the groom in her son [[franciscus_pardon]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe
2 CONT nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). A *dagloonster* of Winksele, present and consenting, and
2 CONT like her husband [[guilielmus_pardon]] recorded as unable to write.
2 CONT
2 CONT The act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date, and the death entry says
2 CONT only that she was alive on the day.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surname is a rare one and its spelling is unsettled — *Pergijsels* is what the act
2 CONT writes, and Pergijssels, Pergisels and Peregijsels all occur in Brabant. That rarity is
2 CONT worth more than it looks: a surname this uncommon is exactly the kind that can be searched
2 CONT on its own, where Bossin and Pardon cannot.
