1 FAMS @F123@
1 NOTE STRONG LEAD, NOT GRAFTED (July 2026) — see [[francl_s]] for the whole of it. A Brugge
2 CONT marriage act of 1851 gives an Anna Francisca **Morbeé**, daughter of Petrus Josephus Morbeé
2 CONT and Joanna De Clerck, marrying a Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert. The forenames and the
2 CONT husband match; the surname does not.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morree and Morbeé are a plausible pair to confuse in a nineteenth-century hand — the double
2 CONT r and the rb are near-identical in cursive — and this record's spelling comes from a member
2 CONT tree, not from an act. That makes the act the better authority in principle, but "in
2 CONT principle" is not evidence, so nothing is changed here. Her son's 1857 Oostende birth act
2 CONT would settle which spelling the registrar used.
