1 NOTE DEEPEST-TIER ANCESTOR — born ~1500, Oostkamp. Father of Barbara Wittenheyns (~1535). The Wittenheyns of Oostkamp appear on two independent lines of ours (also
2 CONT [[mattheus_wittenheyns]] ~1500, via the Vandewalle line); whether Petrus and Mattheus
2 CONT are brothers is not established. No parents recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHECKED AND REJECTED (July 2026) — the duplicate detector flags Petrus and Mattheus as
2 CONT possibly one person, on a rare surname plus a birth year of about 1500. They are not.
2 CONT Four things separate them, and none is a spelling difference:
2 CONT
2 CONT - different given names — Mattheus and Petrus are not variants of one another;
2 CONT - different wives — Judoca 't Jonck here, Maria De Ruwe there;
2 CONT - different deaths — before 1575 here, about 1546 at Oostkamp there;
2 CONT - different children — Barbara (~1535) here; Mattheus's children are named with him in
2 CONT   the 1547 Bruges orphan register.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two men of one uncommon surname, born about the same time in the same parish, is what a
2 CONT pair of brothers or cousins looks like. The warning is expected to keep firing, because
2 CONT it is derived from surname and year alone; this note is the answer to it.
